# Silent Auction Database Schema

**Source of truth:** `database.sql` (DDL) and `seed.sql` (seed data).  
**Database name:** `silent_auction`

## Naming Conventions

- DDL uses **PascalCase** table and column names (`Donor`, `DonorID`).
- PHP queries in `silent_auction_merged/data/` use **lowercase** table names (`donor`, `item`, …).
- Column names stay PascalCase in both (`DonorID`, `TaxReceipt`).
- On Windows MySQL, case-insensitive table names resolve both forms. On Linux, align `lower_case_table_names` or rename tables.

## Tables

### Donor

| Column       | Type                   | Notes                      |
| ------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------- |
| DonorID      | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                            |
| BusinessName | VARCHAR(75)            | nullable                   |
| ContactName  | VARCHAR(75)            |                            |
| ContactEmail | VARCHAR(200)           |                            |
| ContactTitle | VARCHAR(75)            | nullable                   |
| Address      | VARCHAR(75)            |                            |
| City         | VARCHAR(30)            |                            |
| State        | VARCHAR(2)             |                            |
| ZipCode      | VARCHAR(5)             |                            |
| TaxReceipt   | BOOLEAN                | `0` = not sent, `1` = sent |

### Bidder

| Column     | Type                   | Notes          |
| ---------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |
| BidderID   | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                |
| Name       | VARCHAR(75)            |                |
| Address    | VARCHAR(75)            |                |
| CellNumber | VARCHAR(10)            |                |
| HomeNumber | VARCHAR(10)            | nullable       |
| Email      | VARCHAR(200)           |                |
| Paid       | BOOLEAN                | payment status |

### Category

| Column      | Type                   | Notes |
| ----------- | ---------------------- | ----- |
| CategoryID  | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |       |
| Description | VARCHAR(75)            |       |

### Lot

| Column        | Type                   | Notes                         |
| ------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| LotID         | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                               |
| Description   | VARCHAR(75)            |                               |
| CategoryID    | INT                    | → Category                    |
| WinningBid    | DECIMAL(10,2)          | nullable until auction closes |
| WinningBidder | INT                    | → Bidder; nullable            |
| Delivered     | BOOLEAN                | item delivered to winner      |
| Image         | VARCHAR(500)           | nullable                      |

### Item

| Column      | Type                   | Notes                                                  |
| ----------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| ItemID      | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                                                        |
| Description | VARCHAR(75)            |                                                        |
| RetailValue | DECIMAL(10,2)          |                                                        |
| DonorID     | INT                    | → Donor                                                |
| LotID       | INT                    | → Lot; **NULL** = unassigned (awaiting lot assignment) |

### Bid _(optional)_

Only needed for live self-service bidding. Composite PK.

| Column   | Type          | Notes      |
| -------- | ------------- | ---------- |
| LotID    | INT           | → Lot      |
| BidderID | INT           | → Bidder   |
| BidTime  | DATETIME      | part of PK |
| Bid      | DECIMAL(10,2) |            |

## Relationships

```
Donor 1──* Item *──0..1 Lot *──1 Category
                Lot *──0..1 Bidder (WinningBidder)
                Lot 1──* Bid *──1 Bidder
```

- Deleting a donor is blocked when items reference it (FK guard in app).
- Items with `LotID IS NULL` appear in the lot-assignment UI.
- `TaxReceipt` is set to `1` after tax receipt generation (`db_donors.php`).

## Query Examples

```sql
-- Schema DDL
CREATE TABLE Donor (DonorID INT NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT, ...);

-- PHP data layer (lowercase table names)
SELECT * FROM donor WHERE DonorID = :donor_id;
SELECT i.* FROM item i LEFT JOIN lot l ON i.LotID = l.LotID;
UPDATE donor SET TaxReceipt = 1 WHERE DonorID = :donor_id;
```
